  "paper_id": "ccs-2023-is-modeling-access-control-worth-it-d1041ec9",
  "title": "Is Modeling Access Control Worth It?",
  "abstract": "Implementing access control policies is an error-prone task that can have severe consequences for the security of software applications. Model-driven approaches have been proposed in the literature and associated tools have been developed with the goal of reducing the complexity of this task and helping developers to produce secure software efficiently. Nevertheless, there is a lack of empirical data supporting the advantages of model-driven security approaches over code-centric approaches, which are the de-facto industry standard for software development.",
